WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.360
Привет, Датминс Хэлло-Инрашен.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.220
Велком-то привет русский.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:06.820
Эписот Форри-эйд.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.600
Это 24 июня 2026 года.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:11.800
Ам Оли.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.380
Туда и слесано сгон to be a fan on.

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:15.240
Поехали.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.100
А рвотов дедей из жара.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:19.900
Сейт вытмись лолы.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.340
Жара.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.880
Нау again, однорма спит.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:24.760
Жара.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:24.880
Ра.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.620
This word means heat, especially when the weather feels really hot.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.720
Imagine the sun turning be a yard into a giant frying pan.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.760
That is жара.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:37.660
Repeat after me.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.100
Жара.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.720
Now let's use it in a sentence.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.800
Сегодня сильная жара.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.520
That means today there is strong heat.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.840
Let's build more weather words to help you talk about any day.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.920
Our first one is солнце.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:55.480
Сейт слолы.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:56.920
Солын.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:57.500
Ц.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.340
It means sun.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:00.820
Repeat after me.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:02.000
Солын.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:02.640
Ц.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.740
Now try the sentence.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.000
Солца светит ярко.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.460
That means the sun is shining brightly.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.020
Next we have дождь.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:13.220
Say it with me.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:14.140
Дождь.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:14.860
Дождь.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.940
This word means rain.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:18.420
Repeat after me.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:19.300
Дождь.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:20.040
Дождь.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:21.640
Listen to the sentence.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:23.860
Идет дождь.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.900
Дад means rain is falling.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.040
На умить ветер.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:29.260
Сейт слоли.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:31.680
Ви е те ер.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:32.900
It means wind.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.240
Repeat after me.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.520
Ви е те ер.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.120
Try the sentence.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.020
Сильный ветер дует.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.660
Дад means a strong wind is blowing.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.620
Хиря с облака.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:45.760
Сейт витми.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.300
О, блака.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.900
Дождь means cloud.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.200
Repeat after me.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.340
О, блака.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:53.500
Listen.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.740
Белая облака плорют по небу.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.540
Дад means a white cloud is floating across the sky.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.760
Our next word is температура.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:04.840
Say it slowly.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.600
Тем-пература.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.240
It means temperature.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.240
Repeat after me.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:11.880
Тем-пература.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:13.120
Now the sentence.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.800
Тем-пература высокая.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.900
Дад means the temperature is high.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:18.960
Next comes жарко.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:19.940
Say it's with me.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:20.840
Жарко.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:22.660
This word means hot.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.260
When we talk about the weather.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:25.900
Repeat after me.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:26.800
Жарко.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.560
Try the sentence.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:30.400
На улице жарко.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.260
Дад means it is hot outside.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.500
Our last new word is pro-хладна.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:36.840
Say it slowly.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.920
Про-хладна.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.440
It means cool and pleasant way.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:42.960
Репит after me.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.320
Про-хладна.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:45.300
Listen.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:47.540
Сегодня про-хладна.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.080
Дад means today it is cool.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:52.960
Ременбр гроза from orderly lessons.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.520
Say it again with me.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:55.600
Гроза.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.340
It means thunderstorm.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:58.800
Репит after me.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:02:59.840
Гроза.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.400
The sentence is.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:02.560
Гроза идет.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.900
Дад means a thunderstorm is coming.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.340
На улице лук от вас му граммородия.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.960
Когда friends meet, they often start with как погода.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:43.940
That means how is the weather.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.860
It is a friendly way to begin any chat.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:48.800
Now it is practice time.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.800
For kids, draw a big sun.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.060
A cloud and rain drops on paper.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.920
Label each picture with the Russian word and say it out loud.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.920
For adults, look out the window right now.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.280
Make one simple sentence in Russian about today's weather

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.120
using at least two new words.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.140
Want to know a secret about one of today's words?

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.800
The Russian word, температура,

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.960
and the English word, temperature,

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.360
are actually the same word.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.760
They both come from an old Latin word

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.920
that meant a proper mixture or balance.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:23.380
The idea traveled through Europe in scientific writing

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:26.120
and arrived in both languages in the 1700s

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.920
when people started using thermometers.

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:32.960
Remember that connection the next time you check the weather.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.400
It is your secret shortcut.

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:37.180
It is great today.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.140
Say today's words out loud one more time and there yours.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.260
Share the show with a friend who wants to learn Russian

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.660
and I'll see you next time.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:46.360
Пока!

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.020
And if you'd rather watch, then listen.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.040
Find us on YouTube at NerraRU.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:53.740
Links in the show notes.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.500
